Introducing the **Chaos-Net Lattice**. Instead of training a single model, we construct a hypergraph where each node is a distinct neural architecture derived from a parameterized space. We apply a chaotic iterative mapping to these nodes, using a simple logistic map coefficient to drive divergence. Each iteration spawns a new sub-network by perturbing weights and topology, ensuring every branch is mathematically independent. The lattice structure allows us to track lineage and prune redundant paths. We do not train these networks in parallel; instead, we use a shared knowledge pool where successful components are propagated forward via a directed acyclic graph. This creates a family of solutions that are not just different seeds, but fundamentally distinct computational entities, each exploring a unique solution space. The result is a diverse ensemble that captures the full breadth of possible neural behaviors without redundancy. Use this method to generate a forest of models, each with its own unique decision-making style, ready to tackle your problem from every angle.累
